{"name":"Creed","hex":"#c1a44a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Creed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Old English.","A male given name."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Apostles' Creed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Creed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Creed","blocks":[{"text":"A creed, also known as a confession of faith, a symbol, or a statement of faith, is a statement of the shared beliefs of a community which summarizes its core tenets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Nicaea_icon.jpg/330px-Nicaea_icon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creed"},{"title":"Creed (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Creed is a 2015 American sports drama film directed by Ryan Coogler, who co-wrote the screenplay with Aaron Covington. It is the seventh installment in the Rocky franchise, and serves as a spin-off/sequel to Rocky Balboa (2006). It stars Michael B. Jordan, Sylvester Stallone, Tessa Thompson, Phylicia Rashad, Tony Bellew, and Graham McTavish. In the film, amateur boxer Adonis Creed (Jordan) is trained and mentored by Rocky Balboa (Stallone), the former rival turned friend of Adonis' father, Apollo Creed."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Creed_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creed_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Andreas_Nunzer_%C3%9Cbergabe_der_Augsburger_Konfession_1530.jpg/500px-Andreas_Nunzer_%C3%9Cbergabe_der_Augsburger_Konfession_1530.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Andreas_Nunzer_%C3%9Cbergabe_der_Augsburger_Konfession_1530.jpg/1280px-Andreas_Nunzer_%C3%9Cbergabe_der_Augsburger_Konfession_1530.jpg?utm_sourc